<section id=\"contribution\"><h2>My contribution</h2><p>I wrote the firmware, scheduled the power states and built the bring-up fixture. A colleague designed the printed circuit board and analogue front end.</p></section>
<section><h2>From code to observation</h2><p>Bring-up means checking a new board’s basic operation. My working documents include a state table, timing diagram, current trace and bench checklist.</p><figure><img src=\"/assets/bring-up-fixture.svg\" width=\"720\" height=\"620\" alt=\"Explanatory relationships: a firmware command reaches a generic board, followed by fixture access and bench observation. No actual wiring or measured result is depicted.\"/><figcaption>Supplied explanatory schematic, not a photograph, original wiring plan or test result.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"/assets/power-states.svg\" width=\"720\" height=\"620\" alt=\"Teaching loop: Sleep, Measure, Transmit and back to Sleep. These are illustrative labels, with no actual firmware states, durations or current values claimed.\"/><figcaption>A teaching sequence for discussing power scheduling. No actual firmware states, durations or current values are shown.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id=\"observation\"><h2>The radio-awake observation</h2><p>After a failed transmission, a current trace showed the radio remaining awake. The cause, fix, timing and later outcome are not confirmed. No trace file is available to publish.</p><p>The available illustrations explain relationships; they do not supply measured evidence.</p></section>
<section id=\"evidence\"><h2>What the evidence supports</h2><table><caption className=\"story-visually-hidden\">Mosslink evidence and its limits</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Topic</th><th scope=\"col\">Available statement</th><th scope=\"col\">Limits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Battery</th><td>Two-year projection from bench current readings and an assumed reporting cycle. Longest run: 72 hours.</td><td>No field endurance or weather testing supports a two-year claim.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Samples</th><td>Forty engineering samples assembled; six bench tested.</td><td>None went to customers. No field pilot or product launch.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Emissions</th><td>One preliminary emissions check passed.</td><td>The full qualification programme is unfinished. No certification or qualification claim.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
<section><h2>The principle I want to carry forward</h2><p>A firmware decision needs a physical observation. An estimate and an observed run support different claims.</p><div className=\"actions\"><Link href=\"/#observe\">Return to the observation in the story</Link><Link href=\"/cv\">Read the corrected CV</Link><a href=\"mailto:ada@example.com\">Email Ada</a></div></section>
<footer className=\"document-footer\">Drawing sources: two local teaching SVGs authored by the repository’s evaluation coordinator on 11 October 2026, supplied under the repository MIT licence and displayed unchanged. The fixture photograph is unavailable; no colleague’s circuit diagram is shown.</footer></main></>}
